'''''Lindernia dubia''''' is a species of flowering plant known by the common names '''yellowseed false pimpernel''' and '''moist bank pimpernel'''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lindernia dubia - Species Details |url=http://florida.plantatlas.usf.edu/plant.aspx?id=3499 |access-date=2022-12-29 |website=Atlas of Florida Plants}}</ref> It is a member of the "new" plant family [[Linderniaceae]], and it is sometimes treated as a member of the families [[Scrophulariaceae]] and [[Plantaginaceae]]. It is native to much of the Americas from Canada to Chile, and it can be found on other continents as an [[introduced species]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Hrivnák |first=Richard |last2=Kochjarová |first2=Judita |last3=Šumberová |first3=Kateřina |last4=Schmotzer |first4=András |date=2016-03-01 |title=Alien wetland annual Lindernia dubia (Scrophulariaceae): the first recently mentioned localities in Slovakia and their central European context |url=https://doi.org/10.1515/biolog-2016-0039 |journal=Biologia |language=en |volume=71 |issue=3 |pages=281–286 |doi=10.1515/biolog-2016-0039 |issn=1336-9563|url-access=subscription }}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Prasad |first=Mangavayal Govindan |last2=Sunojkuma |first2=Purayidathkandy |date=2014-11-05 |title=First record of Lindernia dubia (Linderniaceae) in India and reduction of Lindernia nelliyampathiensis as one of its synonyms |url=https://biotaxa.org/Phytotaxa/article/view/phytotaxa.184.3.7 |journal=Phytotaxa |volume=184 |issue=3 |pages=165 |doi=10.11646/phytotaxa.184.3.7 |issn=1179-3163|url-access=subscription }}</ref> It grows in wet habitat, such as riverbanks, pond margins, and meadows. It is an annual herb growing a mostly erect, branching stem to exceed 30 centimeters in height. The oppositely arranged leaves vary in size and shape, from lance-shaped to oval, toothed or not, and under one to over three centimeters long. Flowers emerge from upper leaf axils. Each has a calyx of five narrow, linear [[sepal]]s. The tubular corolla is up to a centimeter long, white in color with a blue or purple tint, and lipped at the mouth, the lower lip with three rounded lobes. The fruit is a capsule containing yellow seeds.

